I'll throw you $500.

00:08:13.662 --> 00:08:13.983
Like,

00:08:14.123 --> 00:08:14.263
hey,

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:15.685
that's business.

00:08:15.804 --> 00:08:16.525
Yeah.

00:08:16.526 --> 00:08:19.767
I think Detroit is a city that's got spirit and it's got heart and it's got,

00:08:19.988 --> 00:08:20.209
like,

00:08:20.209 --> 00:08:26.032
the resilience to be a city again if people are willing to want to communicate,

00:08:26.913 --> 00:08:29.295
learn about the history of Detroit.

00:08:29.295 --> 00:08:30.997
learn about how segregation has kind of,

00:08:31.016 --> 00:08:31.236
like,

00:08:31.536 --> 00:08:32.817
destroyed the city in the past.

00:08:32.818 --> 00:08:33.197
Right.

00:08:33.557 --> 00:08:34.879
People talk about what happened in,

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:35.058
like,

00:08:35.059 --> 00:08:36.379
the 80s and the 90s,

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:36.659
but,

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:36.980
like,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.721
literally in the last 5,

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:39.322
10 years,

00:08:39.381 --> 00:08:41.702
some of these houses were burned down.

00:08:41.783 --> 00:08:42.222
Yeah.

00:08:42.543 --> 00:08:42.783
And so,

00:08:42.884 --> 00:08:43.224
yeah,

00:08:43.283 --> 00:08:44.924
Motor City Grounds Coup Recovery Park,

00:08:45.144 --> 00:08:48.006
we want to provide jobs for returning citizens,

