00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:21.728
So it's something the community really needs.

00:09:35.852 --> 00:09:36.352
Detroit.

00:09:37.653 --> 00:09:41.274
It's become known as the poster child of abandonment in the United States.

00:09:42.954 --> 00:09:45.075
But an effort to change that label is underway,

00:09:45.655 --> 00:09:47.715
thanks to local companies like Detroit Dirt.

00:09:48.256 --> 00:09:53.517
Passion Murray started the company five years ago with the mission to rebuild a greener city from the ground up,

00:09:54.357 --> 00:09:55.898
one compost pile at a time.

00:09:56.698 --> 00:09:57.858
So the Detroit Zoo,

00:09:58.378 --> 00:10:00.339
they come in and they bring about

00:10:01.119 --> 00:10:01.899
20 yards.

00:10:02.179 --> 00:10:02.720
Zoo manure.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:03.920
Zoo manure.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.081
The rhinos,

00:10:05.082 --> 00:10:05.941
the giraffes,

00:10:06.381 --> 00:10:07.082
the good stuff.

00:10:07.102 --> 00:10:09.483
This is giraffe shit?

00:10:09.643 --> 00:10:11.244
This is giraffe shit,

00:10:11.284 --> 00:10:11.484
yeah.

00:10:12.285 --> 00:10:13.225
Thank God for the zoo,

00:10:13.285 --> 00:10:14.886
because they got the good shit.

00:10:14.887 --> 00:10:19.109
It's beautiful.

00:10:19.389 --> 00:10:19.909
Can I eat it?

00:10:20.149 --> 00:10:20.630
Go ahead.

00:10:22.531 --> 00:10:23.651
That's food recovery.

00:10:25.312 --> 00:10:26.413
I'll recover some celery.

00:10:32.172 --> 00:10:34.653
And that's why we need to be recovering food.

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:37.073
You all are crazy for throwing this away.

00:10:40.034 --> 00:10:49.357
Passion has transformed this vacant plot of land into a place where recovered food waste and rhino turds combine to produce fertile soil for Detroit's urban farms.

00:10:49.657 --> 00:10:51.958
So what would you say your goal is with this project?

00:10:52.278 --> 00:10:52.798
My goal,

00:10:53.018 --> 00:10:55.239
I've actually reached my goal,

00:10:55.719 --> 00:10:58.840
which was to get the city to pay attention to the progress.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.901
So now the city can look at this as a scalable model.

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.342
This can be replicated anywhere in the country.

00:11:04.662 --> 00:11:07.644
It's a movement that will turn into our culture.

00:11:08.184 --> 00:11:11.725
So if I can get people in New York and Miami and D.C.

00:11:12.045 --> 00:11:12.546
and L.A.

00:11:13.106 --> 00:11:15.007
all joining together to push,

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:15.787
you know,

00:11:15.807 --> 00:11:16.907
the purpose of this,

00:11:16.908 --> 00:11:19.628
then our whole country is going to start doing it.

00:11:19.649 --> 00:11:20.689
Compost or die.

00:11:20.869 --> 00:11:21.869
Compost or die.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:27.932
Passion asked me to help her take some of that good Detroit dirt to one of the urban farms she supplies.

00:11:28.424 --> 00:11:30.064
He's gonna be my new partner now.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:34.706
Since she started trucking compost around town,

00:11:35.146 --> 00:11:37.787
Passion has seen a lot of changes in the Detroit landscape.

00:11:38.327 --> 00:11:45.129
It's interesting how this city has evolved over the last like five years because you see cranes in the air now.

00:11:46.249 --> 00:11:50.470
So the revitalization of the city is definitely real and true.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.431
And I'm excited because

00:11:52.951 --> 00:11:56.572
I've just kind of watched it evolve over a ten year time frame.

00:11:57.316 --> 00:11:59.038
Are there a lot of urban farms in Detroit?

00:11:59.498 --> 00:12:00.179
Oh god,

00:12:00.259 --> 00:12:00.499
yeah.

