00:12:40.725 --> 00:12:40.945
Right.

00:12:42.786 --> 00:12:45.088
What do you think the future of this neighborhood is going to be?

00:12:45.609 --> 00:12:45.889
Well,

00:12:46.009 --> 00:12:47.050
it's already happening.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.352
What we are afraid of is gentrification.

00:12:49.592 --> 00:12:49.792
Okay.

00:12:50.173 --> 00:12:52.855
You see things posted on Facebook like,

00:12:53.135 --> 00:12:53.656
why pay...

00:12:54.076 --> 00:12:58.319
$1,500 in Ann Arbor when you can pay $900 in the North End.

00:12:58.379 --> 00:12:58.540
Well,

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:00.421
people in the North End who live here,

00:13:00.922 --> 00:13:02.183
$900 is a lot of money.

00:13:02.203 --> 00:13:02.883
Yeah.

00:13:02.884 --> 00:13:03.123
Rent.

00:13:03.323 --> 00:13:03.464
Yeah.

00:13:04.064 --> 00:13:05.285
That's a problem.

00:13:05.525 --> 00:13:05.665
Yeah.

00:13:06.386 --> 00:13:09.629
It's a big problem for the city across the board,

00:13:09.909 --> 00:13:10.830
gentrification.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:12.791
We have two Detroits.

00:13:13.171 --> 00:13:13.592
Okay.

00:13:13.593 --> 00:13:14.873
We have the downtown Detroit,

00:13:14.893 --> 00:13:16.374
and then you have the real Detroit,

00:13:16.594 --> 00:13:17.835
and that's the neighborhood.

00:13:18.095 --> 00:13:18.976
When I go downtown,

00:13:19.096 --> 00:13:20.077
I don't even know it.

00:13:20.417 --> 00:13:20.798
You know,

00:13:21.058 --> 00:13:21.658
it's like,

00:13:22.559 --> 00:13:23.640
where are the black folks at?

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.141
You know,

00:13:25.942 --> 00:13:26.422
and then,

00:13:27.703 --> 00:13:29.024
I mean seriously.

00:13:29.204 --> 00:13:29.325
No,

00:13:29.505 --> 00:13:30.466
she's telling the truth.

00:13:30.467 --> 00:13:32.868
I lived down there for over 10 years.

00:13:32.948 --> 00:13:33.088
Yeah,

00:13:33.869 --> 00:13:34.930
and that's a big change.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.411
It is a drastic change.

00:13:36.412 --> 00:13:37.312
This is my first time here.

00:13:37.412 --> 00:13:38.793
It is a drastic change.

00:13:38.933 --> 00:13:40.454
But in the neighborhood,

00:13:40.815 --> 00:13:45.039
it's completely different in terms of the revitalization.

00:13:45.279 --> 00:13:46.120
We're like,

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:46.820
okay,

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:51.024
when they gonna come and fix these potholes?

00:13:51.244 --> 00:13:54.746
when they're going to come and give us some decent sidewalks.

00:13:55.086 --> 00:13:56.047
Put some lights in the street.

00:13:56.107 --> 00:13:56.987
And put some lights.

00:13:57.908 --> 00:13:58.428
Nationally,

00:13:58.448 --> 00:14:01.910
the focus is on downtown and midtown and corp town.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:03.731
But to her point,

00:14:03.831 --> 00:14:06.413
the neighborhoods that anchor all these places,

00:14:06.673 --> 00:14:12.916
it needs to spread out through all those neighborhoods to push people out who have lived their whole lives here,

00:14:12.917 --> 00:14:14.197
who have had businesses here,

00:14:14.317 --> 00:14:15.578
the ones who did stay.

00:14:16.498 --> 00:14:17.199
It's not fair.

00:14:17.259 --> 00:14:17.619
No.

00:14:17.799 --> 00:14:18.799
It's not fair at all.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:19.480
and um

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:21.402
Some of the people who destroyed it,

00:14:21.883 --> 00:14:24.125
they want to come in and tell people how to fix it.

00:14:24.225 --> 00:14:24.406
Right.

00:14:25.647 --> 00:14:29.452
And one way these newcomers try to quote-unquote fix these neighborhoods

00:14:30.452 --> 00:14:32.113
is by attempting to rename them.

00:14:33.033 --> 00:14:34.354
I met up with Cornetta Lane,

00:14:34.914 --> 00:14:38.436
who fought back against gentrification and stood up for her community.

00:14:38.856 --> 00:14:39.496
My neighborhood,

00:14:39.576 --> 00:14:40.056
Core City,

00:14:40.336 --> 00:14:43.578
was in danger of being rebranded as West Corktown.

00:14:43.718 --> 00:14:46.379
If you put Corktown in the name of a neighborhood,

00:14:47.199 --> 00:14:48.600
it is perceived to be safe,

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:50.080
trendy,

00:14:52.301 --> 00:14:53.082
and up and coming.

00:14:53.302 --> 00:14:53.542
I was,

00:14:53.562 --> 00:14:53.722
like,

00:14:53.762 --> 00:14:55.543
scrolling through my Facebook news feed,

00:14:56.003 --> 00:14:57.624
and I come across an article.

00:14:58.916 --> 00:14:59.576
that reads,

00:14:59.756 --> 00:15:00.536
West Corktown,

00:15:00.957 --> 00:15:02.817
creating Detroit's newest neighborhood.

00:15:03.197 --> 00:15:04.137
They developed a logo,

00:15:04.898 --> 00:15:06.038
and then a website,

00:15:06.598 --> 00:15:09.079
and then a Facebook page of 1,200 likes,

00:15:09.839 --> 00:15:11.059
and then t-shirts.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:14.520
So they were branding Core

00:15:15.541 --> 00:15:16.781
City as something that it wasn't.

00:15:17.061 --> 00:15:17.361
Correct.

00:15:17.541 --> 00:15:17.661
Yeah.

00:15:17.921 --> 00:15:18.521
Correct.

00:15:18.542 --> 00:15:21.982
The type of folks that have come out of Core City,

00:15:22.783 --> 00:15:23.043
you know,

00:15:23.503 --> 00:15:24.803
you got Rosa Parks herself.

00:15:25.103 --> 00:15:25.403
All right.

00:15:26.264 --> 00:15:27.264
You got Stevie Wonder.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:28.841
Those are some really heavy hitters.

00:15:28.842 --> 00:15:28.961
Yeah,

00:15:29.001 --> 00:15:29.582
heavy hitters,

00:15:29.622 --> 00:15:29.822
right?

00:15:30.122 --> 00:15:30.743
So I just,

00:15:31.343 --> 00:15:32.144
I really did,

00:15:32.904 --> 00:15:35.567
I think the people of Core City is what makes

00:15:36.227 --> 00:15:36.727
Core City.

00:15:37.608 --> 00:15:39.370
Cornetta put a stop to the rebranding,

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.110
for now.

00:15:41.291 --> 00:15:43.713
And in an effort to further knit her community together,

00:15:44.013 --> 00:15:47.176
she started a neighborhood bike tour called Core City Stories.

00:15:47.736 --> 00:15:49.678
Was Core City always a struggling area?

00:15:50.098 --> 00:15:50.579
It had its,

00:15:50.639 --> 00:15:50.859
like,

00:15:50.999 --> 00:15:53.181
glorious days and also its dark days.

00:15:53.401 --> 00:15:53.641
Okay.

00:15:53.761 --> 00:15:55.423
And I feel right now we're on a rebound.

00:15:55.763 --> 00:15:56.323
People who...

00:15:57.428 --> 00:15:58.488
I live in this area,

00:15:58.869 --> 00:16:00.029
first of all they're resilient,

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.351
and second of all they are committed to seeing,

00:16:06.252 --> 00:16:06.472
you know,

00:16:06.552 --> 00:16:07.812
better days in Cora City.

00:16:08.232 --> 00:16:12.494
It's of my opinion that the people in Detroit don't want Detroit to look like that.

00:16:12.854 --> 00:16:14.055
Of course,

00:16:14.056 --> 00:16:14.475
of course.

00:16:14.555 --> 00:16:16.576
And it's not that their fault.

00:16:16.916 --> 00:16:17.076
Yeah.

00:16:17.536 --> 00:16:21.078
And it takes more than just the people that live in the neighborhood to do it,

00:16:21.079 --> 00:16:21.278
you know.

00:16:21.298 --> 00:16:22.958
It's like you need bigger resources.

00:16:23.178 --> 00:16:24.419
To knock that place down,

00:16:24.939 --> 00:16:25.779
you need machinery.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:26.240
Yeah,

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:26.880
for sure.

00:16:31.748 --> 00:16:33.069
We're in North Corktown right now,

00:16:33.309 --> 00:16:34.991
and Cornetta wants to introduce me to Mr.

00:16:35.051 --> 00:16:35.331
King,

00:16:35.911 --> 00:16:37.633
the unofficial mayor of North Corktown.

00:16:38.233 --> 00:16:40.035
I heard you're the unofficial mayor of this area.

00:16:40.515 --> 00:16:40.715
Yeah,

00:16:41.416 --> 00:16:42.317
I believe I am,

00:16:42.397 --> 00:16:42.557
though,

00:16:42.597 --> 00:16:43.658
because like I said,

00:16:44.178 --> 00:16:46.380
I helps all the neighbors out,

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:46.660
you know,

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.441
the seniors,

00:16:47.661 --> 00:16:49.342
the ones they cannot afford,

00:16:49.382 --> 00:16:49.983
they snow.

00:16:51.064 --> 00:16:51.844
I do they snow.

00:16:52.525 --> 00:16:53.906
I feel good about that.

00:16:54.266 --> 00:16:55.167
My mother taught me,

00:16:55.168 --> 00:16:56.568
you come in this world with nothing,

00:16:56.569 --> 00:16:57.949
you leave this world with nothing,

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.491
but only a kind word to be said.

00:17:00.651 --> 00:17:01.232
Now this is...

00:17:01.512 --> 00:17:02.632
What we be doing,

00:17:03.212 --> 00:17:04.833
we pass our produce.

00:17:05.173 --> 00:17:06.293
Got my bell peppers,

00:17:06.573 --> 00:17:07.814
got fresh eggs,

00:17:08.294 --> 00:17:09.534
other little what not.

00:17:09.535 --> 00:17:09.854
Nice.

00:17:10.295 --> 00:17:10.975
Potatoes.

00:17:11.475 --> 00:17:15.356
And we service the community and anyone we can.

00:17:16.296 --> 00:17:18.817
This used to be the most beautiful neighborhood.

00:17:19.137 --> 00:17:19.977
Garages,

00:17:20.397 --> 00:17:21.098
houses,

00:17:21.678 --> 00:17:22.718
kids playing,

00:17:23.118 --> 00:17:24.439
running up and down the street,

00:17:24.479 --> 00:17:25.679
playing hango seat.

00:17:25.759 --> 00:17:27.599
Got guys standing on the corner.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.520
We used to call that crooning.

00:17:30.032 --> 00:17:34.074
Standing on the corner singing Temptations and all that,

00:17:34.134 --> 00:17:34.454
you know.

00:17:35.995 --> 00:17:37.336
But all that is gone now,

00:17:37.436 --> 00:17:37.556
so,

00:17:37.716 --> 00:17:38.056
you know,

00:17:38.837 --> 00:17:40.158
we're trying to bring it back.

00:17:40.338 --> 00:17:43.739
Have you heard that some people wanted to change the name of the area here?

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:44.100
Yeah,

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:44.920
I heard that.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:48.462
I heard it from a few of the residents.

00:17:48.822 --> 00:17:49.663
This is history,

00:17:49.803 --> 00:17:51.184
so that's why they should leave it.

00:17:51.324 --> 00:17:51.564
You know,

00:17:51.624 --> 00:17:52.644
don't change the name.

00:17:53.085 --> 00:17:54.205
When you change the name,

00:17:54.245 --> 00:17:55.926
what name do you want it to be?

00:17:56.246 --> 00:17:56.526
Right.

00:17:56.586 --> 00:17:58.588
That's another form of control.

00:17:59.856 --> 00:18:00.516
So let it go.

00:18:01.037 --> 00:18:01.157
Yeah.

00:18:01.537 --> 00:18:02.178
Let's live.

00:18:02.538 --> 00:18:02.678
Well,

00:18:02.679 --> 00:18:03.959
we appreciate you taking the time.

00:18:04.139 --> 00:18:04.279
Hey,

00:18:04.399 --> 00:18:04.779
thank you.

00:18:04.819 --> 00:18:06.781
And I appreciate y'all appreciating me.

00:18:14.146 --> 00:18:15.627
If Detroit had a zodiac sign,

00:18:15.647 --> 00:18:16.087
what would it be?

00:18:16.247 --> 00:18:16.888
Oh,

00:18:17.188 --> 00:18:17.968
that's so good.

00:18:18.469 --> 00:18:20.410
It would probably be a Capricorn,

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.691
because Capricorns work hard.

00:18:23.032 --> 00:18:23.152
OK.

00:18:23.592 --> 00:18:24.052
And

00:18:25.013 --> 00:18:29.236
Detroit, we're working hard to be the best city that we can.

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.882
And few are working harder for their city than Cornetta.

00:18:33.923 --> 00:18:35.825
She doesn't just live in this neighborhood,

00:18:36.425 --> 00:18:37.246
she lives for it.

00:18:37.926 --> 00:18:40.609
And in a rapidly evolving landscape like Detroit,

00:18:41.269 --> 00:18:42.850
if you don't stand up for your neighborhood,

00:18:43.531 --> 00:18:44.192
you could lose it.

00:18:45.773 --> 00:18:47.835
We're back home Yay

00:18:48.835 --> 00:18:50.917
What do you think when you hear people say that,

00:18:52.398 --> 00:18:52.639
you know,

00:18:52.659 --> 00:18:55.821
Detroit's sort of a blank slate and they can come here and do whatever they want?

00:18:56.922 --> 00:18:57.042
So,

00:18:57.322 --> 00:18:58.103
unfortunately,

00:18:58.604 --> 00:18:58.904
um...

00:18:59.504 --> 00:19:01.305
People that are outside of Detroit,

00:19:01.505 --> 00:19:04.706
they hear news from people who just moved to Detroit saying,

00:19:05.267 --> 00:19:05.607
oh,

00:19:05.847 --> 00:19:07.347
like you can do anything you want,

00:19:07.407 --> 00:19:09.248
like a land of opportunity.

00:19:11.029 --> 00:19:15.571
And while there are tons of opportunities to take advantage of here,

00:19:16.071 --> 00:19:17.512
Detroit is not a blank slate.

00:19:17.992 --> 00:19:18.632
Detroit,

00:19:18.832 --> 00:19:19.213
rather,

00:19:19.473 --> 00:19:22.494
is a canvas that is missing pieces to it.

00:19:23.194 --> 00:19:25.595
And if you could find yourself in Detroit,

00:19:26.656 --> 00:19:26.936
you know.

00:19:27.632 --> 00:19:36.482
Painting along those edges and kind of like being a piece of the puzzle and not trying to like create a whole new puzzle.

00:19:36.483 --> 00:19:38.584
You know,

00:19:38.644 --> 00:19:41.487
that's that's the type of residence that Detroit needs.

00:19:54.237 --> 00:19:57.018
While many see Detroit's crumbling buildings as eyesores,

00:19:58.799 --> 00:20:01.600
there are those who recognize them as creative opportunities.

00:20:03.221 --> 00:20:03.821
This is creepy.

00:20:04.521 --> 00:20:04.681
Yeah.

00:20:07.162 --> 00:20:08.563
Look out for holes in the ground.

00:20:08.723 --> 00:20:09.363
There's a lot of them.

00:20:10.984 --> 00:20:12.044
I'm here with my friend Justin,

00:20:12.045 --> 00:20:13.285
who's a local Detroit skater.

00:20:14.005 --> 00:20:20.108
And what he does is he goes into some of these buildings and builds some skate spots in them sometimes.

00:20:20.808 --> 00:20:20.928
Yeah?

00:20:26.791 --> 00:20:27.791
When did you first come in here?

00:20:28.491 --> 00:20:30.732
First time I came in here was about six years ago.

00:20:31.252 --> 00:20:33.053
It's changed a lot since that time.

00:20:33.353 --> 00:20:34.874
These buildings are constantly changing,

00:20:34.914 --> 00:20:37.355
evolving from just being exposed to the weather,

00:20:37.635 --> 00:20:38.695
especially scrappers.

00:20:38.795 --> 00:20:40.916
You can see that the roof here,

00:20:41.096 --> 00:20:41.617
like the ceiling,

00:20:41.657 --> 00:20:42.597
is fire damaged.

00:20:43.177 --> 00:20:44.338
And yes,

00:20:44.358 --> 00:20:46.899
there's been a lot of fires and just things that are torn down.

00:20:47.259 --> 00:20:48.679
You made this more skatable or?

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:48.960
Yeah,

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:49.340
actually,

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:49.860
we ended up

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.661
pouring over 2,000 pounds of cement on this.

00:20:53.101 --> 00:20:56.663
I had to get new shocks on my car after doing this project because all the cement that

00:20:57.063 --> 00:20:59.964
I hauled in my car to bring it here.

00:21:00.505 --> 00:21:06.327
It's a pretty time consuming and back breaking process and it's still such a hard thing to skate,

00:21:06.467 --> 00:21:09.129
but it's skatable now and it's cool.

00:21:09.829 --> 00:21:11.029
If you're able to do something on it,

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:12.970
it's pretty sweet.

00:21:24.801 --> 00:21:24.941
Oh,

00:21:25.201 --> 00:21:27.242
it's gone.

00:21:35.986 --> 00:21:43.570
You know

00:21:43.571 --> 00:21:43.890
what sucks?

00:21:43.891 --> 00:21:44.890
This ref right here.

00:21:54.912 --> 00:21:56.973
Watch your head.

00:21:56.993 --> 00:21:57.813
We're up on the roof,

00:21:58.614 --> 00:22:00.695
walking around on a very weak wooden floor,

00:22:01.655 --> 00:22:03.877
and it looks like there's another skate spot up here.

00:22:05.417 --> 00:22:06.498
It's looking pretty weathered.

00:22:07.999 --> 00:22:09.339
I don't know if it survived the winter.

00:22:13.416 --> 00:22:28.286
We've probably done work and built stuff in about 10 different buildings around the city and I feel like we're able to like you know do a little creative reuse like it's these forgotten things that no one cares about and now we're making something useful out of them kind of bringing them back to life.

00:22:28.286 --> 00:22:29.568
to life in a way.

00:22:29.808 --> 00:22:31.650
You just have a lot of freedom to do what you like.

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:35.134
And that's a big part of skateboarding is creativity and just imagining what if,

00:22:35.655 --> 00:22:36.556
what can you do here,

00:22:36.696 --> 00:22:37.477
what's possible.

00:22:37.978 --> 00:22:41.242
And if you're willing to put in the time and the effort and the work,

00:22:41.322 --> 00:22:43.244
which is a lot of times just super duper.

00:22:43.264 --> 00:22:44.064
dirty and grueling,

00:22:44.665 --> 00:22:45.525
you can make it happen.

00:22:45.825 --> 00:22:46.886
It's really just up to you.

00:22:47.606 --> 00:22:56.311
These buildings give a lot of possibility that might not be a possibility outside in the streets where things we build will get demolished pretty fast.

00:22:56.771 --> 00:22:58.793
Here they have some kind of lifespan,

00:22:59.373 --> 00:23:03.095
but that lifespan is always unknown.

00:23:05.036 --> 00:23:06.257
It's really up to the elements,

00:23:06.817 --> 00:23:11.239
up to the scrappers and the others that wander the building how long our stuff lasts.

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.601
I think it's cool that hard work is still being done in this building,

00:23:17.081 --> 00:23:18.281
years after it was closed.

00:23:19.262 --> 00:23:20.302
And in their own small way,

00:23:20.842 --> 00:23:24.263
Justin and his friends are contributing to Detroit's revitalization.

00:23:26.063 --> 00:23:26.884
Over in Midtown,

00:23:27.124 --> 00:23:29.784
they wanted to show me another DIY park they helped build,

00:23:30.205 --> 00:23:31.385
at an abandoned rec center.

00:23:32.845 --> 00:23:33.726
Welcome to The Wig.

00:23:45.016 --> 00:23:46.897
No matter what I do,

00:23:47.097 --> 00:23:49.519
they say I waste my days.

00:23:53.642 --> 00:23:57.665
If I was killing hookers on the English Bay,

00:24:02.208 --> 00:24:09.934
they'd say at least it's something for a man to do.

00:24:15.648 --> 00:24:16.949
So how long has this been going on for?

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:17.830
About a year and a half now.

00:24:18.030 --> 00:24:18.150
OK.

00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:19.271
Since we took over.

00:24:19.591 --> 00:24:21.052
That's how the city's coming back right now,

00:24:21.132 --> 00:24:21.252
is,

00:24:21.432 --> 00:24:21.913
you know,

00:24:22.153 --> 00:24:25.235
the youth and the people that care stepping up and saying,

00:24:25.275 --> 00:24:27.396
you know,

00:24:27.397 --> 00:24:27.937
I'm taking this.

